- Story & Context: Three months after the road dispute ended in an injunction, local farmhands and drift musicians held an equinox dinner directly across the decommissioned lanes of Blackwood Cut. Under rows of kerosene lanterns, bread loaves were baked directly upon the warm steel covers of idling electrical enclosures, filling the cool night air with the scent of charred caraway seeds and ozone. When Silas plugged a hurdy-gurdy into the abandoned crosswalk circuit, the dead median speakers woke up on their own, harmonizing with the autumn wind in an unearthly modal drone that echoed the hook, "Pass the broken bread across the yellow line." Truckers on the distant bypass claimed their radios picked up the communal song for weeks afterward, humming out from the unpowered ditch like an eternal ghost in the asphalt.
